The vendored Eigen 3-by-3 tridiagonalization specialization in
`vendor/eigen/Eigen/src/Eigenvalues/Tridiagonalization.h` is modified by PDG
only to add Eigen's existing `EIGEN_DEVICE_FUNC` annotation. This permits the
same fixed-size self-adjoint QR eigensolver used by upstream PDAL to compile
for CUDA without substituting a numerically different solver. The file remains
Copyright (c) 2008 Gael Guennebaud and Copyright (c) 2010 Jitse Niesen and is
distributed under the Mozilla Public License 2.0 stated in that source file.

The vendored `vendor/eigen/Eigen/src/Core/MathFunctions.h` also carries
Eigen's merged change !1363, "Fix use of arg function in CUDA." It replaces
the nonstandard device-global `::arg` lookup with `std::arg`, fixing Eigen
3.4.0 compilation under NVCC, MSVC, and C++20. The file remains distributed
under Eigen's Mozilla Public License 2.0 terms and retained source notice.

